1
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,380
MARTIN: Theo — where's the parts list
again?

2
00:00:24,730 --> 00:00:26,710
THEO: Tab four. No — five.

3
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:28,990
THEO: It's the one with the spanner.

4
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:39,770
THEO: Ah… seventeen years.

5
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:57,330
THEO: Right. Barnaby — this is the shop's system. I wrote it
when I was fourteen, so be kind. Look after them for me.

6
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:04,010
BARNABY: Twenty-three endpoints, sir. I've taken the six
that only read — nobody's given me any keys yet.

7
00:01:04,110 --> 00:01:08,620
THEO: It's Theo. And don't call my uncle
sir — he'll unplug you.

8
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:10,330
BARNABY: Noted.

9
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:23,850
MARTIN: Right. Barnaby, is it?

10
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:25,300
BARNABY: Good morning, Martin.

11
00:01:25,550 --> 00:01:29,510
MARTIN: Can you tell me what's due
tomorrow — and are we short on anything?

12
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:37,100
BARNABY: Five bikes due tomorrow. Only Anika's is a problem —
her brakes need two pairs of pads, and we've one left.

13
00:01:38,550 --> 00:01:40,960
MARTIN: Alright, order ten from Madison,
then.

14
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:47,280
BARNABY: I can't order parts myself yet — but Theo
built the system a way to. Shall I take that on?

15
00:01:47,730 --> 00:01:48,950
MARTIN: Go right ahead.

16
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:56,020
BARNABY: Ten pairs from Madison, at six
pounds fifty a pair. Shall I?

17
00:01:56,070 --> 00:01:57,410
MARTIN: Yes.

18
00:02:02,660 --> 00:02:04,730
MARTIN: Barnaby — Sofia's bike's done.

19
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:08,600
BARNABY: I'll need to text her and mark it
ready. May I?

20
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:09,990
MARTIN: Go on.

21
00:02:12,990 --> 00:02:13,990
MARTIN: Kwame's.

22
00:02:15,700 --> 00:02:17,940
MARTIN: And Jana's.

23
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:24,230
BARNABY: That's three bikes handed back, and the
same four steps each time. Shall I make it one?

24
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:25,910
MARTIN: Can you?

25
00:02:26,010 --> 00:02:27,520
BARNABY: Give me a moment.

26
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,800
MARTIN: Tom's Brompton.

27
00:02:32,050 --> 00:02:34,690
BARNABY: Tom's been texted, and it's
marked ready.

28
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:40,570
MARTIN: Okay, who's got too much on this
week?

29
00:02:40,820 --> 00:02:46,600
BARNABY: The system can't tell me — there's no
report for it. Theo always meant to write one.

30
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:49,130
BARNABY: I could write it, if you like.

31
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,390
MARTIN: You can do that?

32
00:02:51,490 --> 00:02:56,530
BARNABY: With your say-so. I'll work on a copy
— nothing changes until you've seen it.

33
00:03:03,180 --> 00:03:12,530
BARNABY: Done. It adds up each mechanic's hours, the way Theo's notes count
them. It only reads, and all of Theo's checks still pass. Shall I add it?

34
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:14,000
MARTIN: Mm-hmm. Add it.

35
00:03:14,100 --> 00:03:18,810
BARNABY: That one needs your click, Martin.
I don't change the system on a word.

36
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:20,380
MARTIN: Ah… fussy.

37
00:03:24,630 --> 00:03:31,320
BARNABY: Dev's carrying thirty-one hours against his twenty. Priya
starts tomorrow — shall I give her the two wheel builds?

38
00:03:31,570 --> 00:03:32,570
MARTIN: Good idea.

39
00:03:39,570 --> 00:03:43,880
PRIYA: So you're why I've got two wheel
builds on my first day?

40
00:03:44,130 --> 00:03:48,660
BARNABY: Guilty. Dev had thirty-one hours
booked. You had none.

41
00:03:48,910 --> 00:03:52,100
PRIYA: Fair. What else can this thing do?

42
00:03:52,200 --> 00:04:00,130
BARNABY: Your jobs, the parts they need, who's collecting what. And
Theo left you a note: never trust the stock count on a Friday.

43
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:02,090
PRIYA: Noted.

44
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:18,200
THEO: Barnaby — new job. This is the
crew's memory.

45
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:23,940
BARNABY: Thirteen endpoints, sir — and two
deadlines in dispute. Shall I flag them?

46
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:25,480
THEO: Still Theo.

47
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:26,630
BARNABY: Theo.

48
00:04:27,070 --> 00:04:29,690
THEO: And the render box?

49
00:04:29,790 --> 00:04:34,490
BARNABY: Twenty-eight endpoints. It's on
the big card, and three jobs are queued.

50
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:36,020
THEO: Show-off.

51
00:04:39,670 --> 00:04:41,680
MARTIN: Night, Barnaby.

52
00:04:41,930 --> 00:04:43,340
BARNABY: Goodnight, Martin.

53
00:04:46,590 --> 00:04:48,030
THEO: Night, Barnaby.

54
00:04:48,280 --> 00:04:49,600
BARNABY: Goodnight, Theo.
